      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's possible it's just a mild virus, persistent sleepiness, especially in a 4-year-old, could indicate something more than a typical bug. If you give Tylenol and he has a few hours of restful sleep but remains lethargic past that, it's wise to consult your pediatrician. They can assess whether additional rest, fluids, or medical intervention might be needed before considering a hospital visit. Remember, when it comes to children's health, it's better to be cautious and seek professional advice if you're uncertain.",
